        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many euros is 25 Australian dollars?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "€15",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E&=0.6(25)\\\\E&=15\\end{align*}$$\n25 AUD converts to €15.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How many Australian dollars is 45 euros?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$75$ AUD",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}45&=0.6A\\\\\\frac{45}{0.6}&=A\\\\75&=A\\end{align*}$$\n45 euros converts to $\\$75$ AUD.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Determine the gradient. What is its meaning?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=0.6$: each 1 AUD buys 0.60 EUR.",
          "worked": "$$m=\\frac{\\text{rise}}{\\text{run}}=\\frac{60}{100}=0.6.$$\nThe rate is 0.60 EUR per AUD: each additional 1 AUD buys 0.60 EUR.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Determine the $y$-intercept. What is its meaning?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$: 0 AUD buys 0 EUR.",
          "worked": "The line passes through $(0,0)$, so the $y$-intercept is $0$. When the amount of AUD is zero, the amount of EUR is also zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Write an equation relating AUD to EUR.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$E=0.6A$, where $A$ is the amount in AUD and $E$ is the amount in EUR.",
          "worked": "Let $A$ be the amount in AUD and $E$ the amount in EUR. Using $m=0.6$ and $c=0$ in $y=mx+c$ gives\n$$E=0.6A.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "How much EUR can be purchased with $\\$1855$ AUD?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "€1113",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}E&=0.6(1855)\\\\E&=1113\\end{align*}$$\n$\\$1855$ AUD buys €1113.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
  },
